  "definition": "Physics Simulation is the computational modelling of physical phenomena \u2014 including rigid-body dynamics, soft-body deformation, fluid behaviour, and collision detection \u2014 to produce physically plausible behaviour in virtual environments. It underpins interactive experiences in virtual reality, robotics training, and digital-twin applications by enabling real-time or near-real-time approximations of classical mechanics.",
